      "subject": "Issue 1247: Keep numeric_range consistent with the items it produces",
      "body": "numeric_range produces its items by repeated multiplication, but derived\nlen(), __contains__ and index() from division by the step. With floats the\ntwo disagree, so a range could report a length that did not match what it\nyielded, and could deny membership to its own items.\n\nSettle all of them against the items themselves: _len trims or extends the\ndivided count until it matches the values produced, and index() confirms\nthe candidate position by comparing against the item at that position.\n__contains__ and count() now follow index(), so the four cannot drift apart\nagain.\n\nExact types are unaffected: their remainders are already zero, so they take\nthe same path and the same number of operations as before.",
      "source_files": [
        "more_itertools/more.py"
      ],
      "test_files": [
        "tests/test_more.py"
      ],
      "deleted_source": [],
      "lines_changed": 53,
      "test_ids": [
